; When an option's argument is missing, whether "--name=" gives an empty value
; or a short-option cluster ends on a letter that takes an argument with no
; argv word after it, the one diagnostic is the option handler's "No argument
; provided".  option-argument-forms.test pins the forms that succeed.

2024/01/01 Test
    Expenses:Food   $10.00
    Assets:Cash

test bal --limit= -> 1
__ERROR__
Error: No argument provided for --limit
end test

test bal -El -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing option '-l'
Error: No argument provided for --limit
end test
